#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a38549-e9d0-5292-b347-f74fdc9a6a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358372} {:answer/id #uuid "9a7e7195-94cf-5506-a52a-8100b8c7530e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358373} {:answer/id #uuid "6e41d8f9-9932-5363-9d70-893d355df9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358374} {:answer/id #uuid "c286cd82-b436-58c7-b0e8-65f82759ab73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358375} {:answer/id #uuid "ea03050c-8116-5e3e-8e00-cec46213345b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04a38549-e9d0-5292-b347-f74fdc9a6a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358372} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9ee173-a796-55ff-b6c6-51ac496eba73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "53b08071-c3b4-5e7f-a8d9-b603030484cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-325108" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.25,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.25$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d409b5f5-fa03-5933-8bbc-fede9019aaa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358379} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6a3172-acd6-50f0-af59-4f96e0c28f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358380} {:answer/id #uuid "374b4429-1b0c-5e0b-9681-2a9fe144a40d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358381} {:answer/id #uuid "83673c7d-d438-5ff8-9d86-99ce446ec553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358382} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f8eae1-0150-5566-a1ff-b5ed868210e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83673c7d-d438-5ff8-9d86-99ce446ec553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358382} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa36696-176b-5d34-a5ba-f5dacde941ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2538be23-7392-567d-ae84-6157c02bc118" :question/math-academy-id "q-333098" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x\\,y-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.25,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side to define $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.25$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03235b38-4b62-51da-b0fe-5cda64becd99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358386} {:answer/id #uuid "734f6b6c-d641-5eae-9eae-86eb1f9d01a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358387} {:answer/id #uuid "7beb27be-16fb-5257-b777-20cfab38efc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358388} {:answer/id #uuid "58885867-92b1-52af-a618-eb09284f397a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{x}_{\\text{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358389} {:answer/id #uuid "0bda7078-af52-5548-9659-2abf600878cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bda7078-af52-5548-9659-2abf600878cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358390} :answer-field/id #uuid "396beca5-39ea-5f3b-a418-c8882472e609" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e03e7ca-7137-52f7-b424-499e78b6afe7" :question/math-academy-id "q-333114" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}+x,\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {{{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-y-{x}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.$ Therefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2-1 \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "866481fb-c460-5a39-a7a0-84b64d8bd673" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating the Solution to an Initial Value Problem Using the Implicit Euler Method: One Step"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2928918-59fc-547d-b0d8-de95f5d79ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.07" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358393} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e4a0d3-285f-5b28-b557-4cc20ea03ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2928918-59fc-547d-b0d8-de95f5d79ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.07" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358393} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9fbf995-7485-5d67-afa9-849bbd8afcf6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "446684c1-6fd8-5e60-ae93-0058401c626a" :question/math-academy-id "q-333251" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-xy,\\,y(0.5)=1.1\n$$\n\nUse the implicit Euler method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(1).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0.5=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0.5+0.5=1.$ Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5(1){y}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1.1-0.5(1)^{3} \\\\  & =1.5{y}_{\\text{new}}-1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1.1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method. \n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=1.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{1.5({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-1.6}{1.5}\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(0.5)=1.1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1.1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & ≈1.066667 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈1.066667\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈1.07,$ rounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "866481fb-c460-5a39-a7a0-84b64d8bd673" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating the Solution to an Initial Value Problem Using the Implicit Euler Method: One Step"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ca38ed6-0b3b-5496-8119-c9900d922ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ca38ed6-0b3b-5496-8119-c9900d922ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358397} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0c699d-fad0-5505-b00f-25f4383436bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "875d5bc3-0a8e-5296-bc39-00195d13f0a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-333298" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-3x,\\,y(1.5)=-2.5\n$$\n\nUse the implicit Euler method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1.5=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3{x}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1.5+0.5=2.$ Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}-2.5-1.5(2) \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}-5.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=-2.5$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method. \n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-5.5}{(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})-1}\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1.5)=-2.5,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =-2.5 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & =-2.464286 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈-2.464102 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈-2.464102\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-2.46,$ rounded to two decimal places."}]}
